module main

# Stage 0a soundness — the escape check with the return type OMITTED. The sibling
# `existential_escape` declares `-> Int`, which the rigidity scan catches. With no
# annotation the scan has nothing to look at: the synthesized placeholder is not a
# variable the programmer wrote, so it is not in the scheme's binder list and the
# scan never visits it. The skolem rode into the decl's generalized scheme
# instead, and `unbox` was accepted as `main.Boxed -> $sk<n>`.
#
# A skolem is a rigid TConst, so it has no free type variables — generalize's
# ftv-difference never sees it — and being unquantified it is NOT refreshed at
# instantiation. Every call site of `unbox` therefore shared ONE rigid type, and
# `print` (forall a. a -> Unit) happily consumed it: printing a String through
# this helper emitted a raw heap address.

type Boxed = | exists a. Boxed a

fn unbox(b: Boxed) =
  match b with
  | Boxed x -> x

fn main() -> Unit !{IO} =
  print(unbox(Boxed("hi")))
